            "description": "Watch Portugal vs Nigeria highlights and goals from Friendly on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on June 10, 2026. Portugal and Nigeria faced off in an international friendly, testing their tactical setups and physical readiness ahead of their upcoming competitive fixtures. International Showcase on the Pitch On June 10, 2026 , the football world turned its attention to a high-stakes friendly between two of the most exciting teams in global sports. Both Portugal and Nigeria viewed this match as a critical opportunity to fine-tune their rosters, leading to a contest defined by tactical discipline and sudden bursts of individual brilliance. The first half saw both sides trading blows in a balanced display, setting the stage for a dramatic conclusion under the floodlights. Conceição Finds the Decisive Blow As the match entered its final twenty minutes, the intensity spiked. João Félix received a yellow card in the 71st minute as frustration began to show, but the mood shifted instantly just four minutes later. In the 75th minute, João Cancelo delivered a precise assist that found Francisco Conceição , whose clinical finish put Portugal ahead 2-1. The goal sent the home fans into a frenzy, rewarding the sustained pressure the hosts had exerted throughout the second half. Tensions Boil Over in Stoppage Time The closing stages of the match were marked by physical play as Nigeria pushed for an equalizer. The referee was forced to intervene frequently, booking Zaidu Sanusi in the third minute of injury time for a heavy challenge. Shortly after, Portugal 's S. Costa also saw yellow as the match ended in a flurry of activity, securing a vital result for the home side in their preparation for the challenges ahead."
